        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. PB2 Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            PB2 Performance is a real protein powder and a good-value one; Original PB2 and PB2 Pure are powdered peanut butter that happen to contain some protein. Per the labels at the time of writing, Performance gives 20 g of protein per 45 g serving, while Original and Pure give 6 g per 13 g serving.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy PB2 Performance if</strong> you want a dairy-free shake with no added sugar, a short ingredient list and real peanut flavor, and you do not mind about 190 calories per serving. <strong>Skip it if</strong> you need a certified-tested powder for drug-tested sport, if inulin fiber upsets your stomach, or if anyone in your home has a peanut allergy. Use Original or Pure PB2 to flavor a shake, not to build one.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
