        <div id="who" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Who Should Buy PB2 Protein Powder, and Who Should Skip It?
          </h2>

          <p>
            PB2 Performance suits people who want a plant protein shake with no added sugar, real peanut flavor and a short label, and who have room for about 190 calories per serving. It is also a reasonable pick for anyone avoiding dairy, soy and pea protein at once, since its protein comes from peanuts and brown rice.
          </p>

          <p>
            Home bakers do well with the whole range. Performance adds 20 g of protein to pancake or muffin batter with a peanut flavor that survives the oven, and PB2 Pure works like a lower-fat peanut flour in cookies and energy balls. If baking is your main use, our <a href="/best-protein-powder-for-baking/">best protein powder for baking</a> guide explains how plant and peanut powders behave in heat compared with whey.
          </p>

          <p>
            Skip PB2 entirely if anyone in your household has a peanut allergy. Every PB2 peanut product lists peanuts as its main ingredient, and the almond products are made by the same company, so ask PB2 about shared equipment before assuming they are safe for a peanut-allergic person. Skip Performance too if inulin or chicory fiber has given you gas before, or if you need a certified powder for drug-tested sport.
          </p>

          <p>
            People trying to lose weight should weigh the calories. At about 238 calories per 25 g of protein, Performance is fine as a meal-style shake but less efficient than a pea or whey isolate when you just want protein. Our <a href="/how-much-protein-do-i-need/">protein calculator guide</a> helps you size the dose before choosing a powder.
          </p>

          <p>
            Anyone with kidney disease, a history of severe food allergies, pregnancy, or a medication regimen should check with a doctor or registered dietitian before adding a daily protein powder. For everyone else, PB2 Performance is a sound, fairly priced plant option, and it sits alongside the other brands in our <a href="/best-plant-based-protein-powder/">best plant-based protein powders</a> roundup.
          </p>
        </div>

