              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Buyer reviews favor Dutch Cocoa for shakes, with most raters giving it five stars and calling it not chalky and not too sweet, though a few say the chocolate is faint. Vanilla is preferred for mixing into yogurt, oatmeal and baking, where its milder flavor lets the peanut come through. Neither flavor contains added sugar, per the labels.
